  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Define \\(x\\heartsuit y\\) to be \\(|x - y|\\) for all real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) Which of the following statements is not true?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x\\heartsuit y = y\\heartsuit x\\) for all \\(x\\) and \\(y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2(x\\heartsuit y) = (2x)\\heartsuit(2y)\\) for all \\(x\\) and\n\\(y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x\\heartsuit 0 = x\\) for all \\(x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x\\heartsuit x = 0\\) for all \\(x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(x\\heartsuit y \\gt 0\\) if \\(x \\neq y\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2003-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x\\heartsuit 0=|x-0|=|x|,\\) statement (C) claims \\(|x|=x\\) for all \\(x,\\) which fails when \\(x\\lt0.\\) For example, \\((-1)\\heartsuit 0 = 1 \\neq -1.\\)\n\nEvery other statement follows directly from properties of the absolute value.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(x\\heartsuit 0=|x|\\)",
        "Test a negative value of \\(x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
